  "body": "This is a proposal for a new error handling of widgets/connectors' bad usage, with a showcase of `poweredBy`.\r\n\r\n## The problem\r\n\r\nWhen using widgets, we currently ignore all errors thrown at the connector level and only re-throw the widget's usage. This is very misleading as a user because you never know what you're doing wrong (showing a complete usage doesn't give any clue on what's misused).\r\n\r\nMoreover, having the widget's or the connector's usage in the source code makes it error prone as it has a maintenance cost. Now that we have a single place for [our documentation](https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/what-is-instantsearch/js/) (the Algolia website), we should redirect all our documentation efforts there. Besides, it increases tremendously the bundle size.\r\n\r\n## This solution\r\n\r\nIt gets rid of the verbose usage and links to the documentation website for more details. An error thrown at the connector level is not ignored anymore by the widget.\r\n\r\nWe can implement this strategy to all widgets/connectors if it works for you.\r\n\r\n### Usage in the source code\r\n\r\n#### For a widget\r\n\r\n```js\r\nimport { createDocumentationMessageGenerator } from '../../lib/utils';\r\n\r\nconst withUsage = createDocumentationMessageGenerator('powered-by');\r\n\r\nexport default function poweredBy({ container } = {}) {\r\n  if (!container) {\r\n    throw new Error(withUsage('The \"container\" option is required.'));\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### For a connector\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// ...\r\n\r\nconst withUsage = createDocumentationMessageGenerator('powered-by', {\r\n  connector: true,\r\n});\r\n\r\n// ...\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Output for the user\r\n\r\n#### Example of error for a widget\r\n\r\n```\r\nThe \"container\" option is required.\r\n\r\nSee documentation: https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/powered-by/js/\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Example of error for a connector\r\n\r\n```\r\nThe render function is not valid (got type \"undefined\").\r\n\r\nSee documentation: https://www.algolia.com/doc/api-reference/widgets/powered-by/js/#connector\r\n```",
